          "snippet": "on the organism.\n\nHowever, the general structures and functions of\nthe protein synthesis machinery are comparable from bacteria to human cells. Translation requires the input of an\nmRNA template, ribosomes, tRNAs, and various enzymatic factors. (Note: A ribosome can be thought of as an\nenzyme whose amino acid binding sites are specified by mRNA.)\nLINK TO LEARNING\nClick through the steps of this PB",
          "score": 0.7695415211818426
