          "chunk_id": "chunk:ch15_genes_and_proteins:6",
          "text": "of this\ninformation for protein synthesis, while keeping the DNA itself intact and protected.\n\nThe copying\nof DNA to RNA is relatively straightforward, with one nucleotide being added to the mRNA strand\nfor every nucleotide read in the DNA strand. The translation to protein is a bit more complex\nbecause three mRNA nucleotides correspond to one amino acid in the polypeptide sequence. However, the translation to protein is still systematic and colinear, such that nucleotides 1 to 3\ncorrespond to amino acid 1, nucleotides 4 to 6 correspond to amino acid 2, and so on. 392\n15 • Genes and Proteins\nAccess for free at openstax.org",
